        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    company_a = [120, 125, 130, 128, 135, 138, 140, 142, 145, 147, 150, 152]\n    company_b = [100, 105, 110, 107, 112, 115, 118, 120, 123, 125, 130, 132]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    correlation = calculate_pearson_correlation(company_a, company_b)\n    answer = round(correlation, 2)\n\n    # return answer\n    return answer\n\n\ndef calculate_pearson_correlation(x_values, y_values):\n    n = len(x_values)\n    numerator = n * sum(x * y for x, y in zip(x_values, y_values)) - sum(x_values) * sum(y_values)\n    denominator = (\n        (n * sum(x ** 2 for x in x_values) - sum(x_values) ** 2)\n        * (n * sum(y ** 2 for y in y_values) - sum(y_values) ** 2)\n    ) ** 0.5\n    return numerator / denominator\n```",
